1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:01,600
Phase 0: Collecting Humans Before You Have Anything to Offer Them Here's the problem.

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:07,440
You want to end war and disease. You don't have a nonprofit, registered securities, or a bank account.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,600
What you do have is an argument and the audacity to think that might be enough.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,500
This is Phase 0. The goal isn't money (you can't legally accept it yet).

5
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:25,860
The goal is building a database of every human who agrees that dying from preventable causes is a strange thing to tolerate.

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,660
You're collecting proof of demand before you have a product.

7
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:37,080
It's a Kickstarter where the reward is "possibly not dying," which is, when you think about it, the most compelling reward

8
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:45,720
tier in crowdfunding history. The Bootstrapping Problem. Before you can accept donations, you need five zero one c three

9
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,800
status. Before you can sell bonds, you need S.E.C. registration.

10
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:56,700
Before you can do either, you need a bank account. It's bureaucratic nesting dolls, each one requiring the previous one

11
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:05,220
to already exist. Humanity has solved this exact problem the same way every time: you collect people first, then point at

12
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:11,320
the crowd when institutions ask "but who wants this?" Abolition, suffrage, civil rights.

13
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:15,500
Someone wrote down names. The names became bargaining power.

14
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:21,140
The bargaining power became policy. It's almost like democracy works when someone remembers to use it.

15
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:30,480
Three Types of Allies. People who want to help fall into three categories, each requiring a slightly different dialect of

16
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:39,400
persuasion. Investors. People who hear "two hundred seventy-two percent annual return backed by health savings" and immediately

17
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,610
open a spreadsheet. Their pupils dilate. Their pulse quickens.

18
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:49,560
They ask about the term structure. They're not heartless. They just process moral arguments faster when those arguments

19
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:53,100
come with compound interest. They'll wait if the math is good.

20
00:01:53,600 --> 00:02:00,140
They will not wait if the math is vibes. Advocates. People motivated by the mission.

21
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:06,940
They share things on social media, write to politicians, volunteer time, and donate money they probably shouldn't.

22
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:11,780
They are, frankly, the only reason your species has ever improved anything.

23
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:16,860
Without them, the spreadsheet people would still be optimizing returns on the slave trade.

24
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:24,560
Give them specific actions they can take right now. Telling someone "care about this" without giving them something to do

25
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:32,300
is how you manufacture apathy. I have watched four thousand two hundred ninety-seven years of humans being told to "raise

26
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:39,880
awareness." Awareness has been raised. The awareness is just sitting there, fully raised, doing nothing.

27
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:47,760
Institutional Partners. Organizations (nonprofits, research institutions, health agencies) that already work on pieces of

28
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:51,600
this problem. They have infrastructure, credibility, and donor bases.

29
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:55,340
You have a framework that could make their existing work more effective.

30
00:02:55,820 --> 00:03:02,660
This is a trade, not a favor. Approach it like one. Nobody wants to be "partnered with" by someone who clearly just wants

31
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:10,320
their mailing list. Institutions are territorial in the way that dogs are territorial, except dogs eventually stop barking.

32
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:19,840
Phase zero Targets. By the end of Phase zero, you want: one hundred thousand plus registered supporters across all three

33
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:25,520
categories. one thousand plus qualified investors with stated investment ranges.

34
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:29,960
one hundred plus institutional partners with expressed interest.

35
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:35,980
one billion plus dollars in stated investment demand (registered, not committed).

36
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:46,190
This database is your ammunition for everything that follows: five zero one c three applications ("here are our supporters").

37
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:52,680
S.E.C. registration ("here is market demand"). Political meetings ("here are your constituents").

38
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:59,020
Platform launch ("here are your users"). Bureaucrats don't respond to arguments.

39
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:03,900
They respond to evidence that other people already responded to arguments.

40
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:09,300
It's like a restaurant: nobody wants to eat there until other people are already eating there.

41
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:14,460
Your entire civilization runs on this principle, and nobody admits it.

42
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:22,280
You literally invented a word for it ("social proof") so you could study it in universities instead of just feeling embarrassed.

43
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:30,080
Getting Started. Build three registration forms (investors, advocates, partners).

44
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:34,280
Takes twenty minutes. Put up a website. The forms and the argument.

45
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:40,320
It does not need to be pretty. No movement in history was stopped because the font was wrong.

46
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:46,380
Start telling people. Social media, Reddit, forums, conferences, your dentist.

47
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:51,380
Especially your dentist. You're already trapped there. They can't leave either.

48
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:55,460
It's the perfect recruiting environment. Send monthly updates.

49
00:04:56,200 --> 00:05:04,340
Real progress, real numbers, real timeline. "three thousand two hundred forty-seven registered investors representing one

50
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:09,500
hundred eighty million dollars in stated interest" beats "the movement is growing!"

51
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:18,860
because adults prefer arithmetic to enthusiasm. The military-industrial complex has a seventy-five-year head start, unlimited

52
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:23,720
budgets, and thousands of lobbyists. You have a spreadsheet and an argument.

53
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:29,760
Historically, that's been enough. (It shouldn't be. But your species is weird like that.).
